      <h1 id="update-cnf-update-prep" class="group scroll-mt-20">Configuring application pods before updating your OpenShift Container Platform cluster<a href="#update-cnf-update-prep" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p class="_abstract">Configure application pods to ensure workload availability during OpenShift Container Platform updates. For example, use deployment strategies, pod disruption budgets, anti-affinity rules, and health probes to maintain high availability and prevent service disruption. In the telecommunications industry, most containerized network function (CNF) vendors follow the guidance in Red Hat best practices for Kubernetes to ensure that the cluster can schedule pods properly during an upgrade.</p>
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Important</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>Always deploy pods in groups by using <code>Deployment</code> resources. <code>Deployment</code> resources spread the workload across all of the available pods ensuring there is no single point of failure. When a pod that is managed by a <code>Deployment</code> resource is deleted, a new pod takes its place automatically.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <section class="related-resources _additional-resources">
      <p class="related-resources-title">Additional resources</p>
      <ul><li><a href="https://redhat-best-practices-for-k8s.github.io/guide/">Red Hat best practices for Kubernetes</a></li></ul>
      </section>
      <h2 id="update-pdb_update-cnf-update-prep" class="group scroll-mt-20">Ensuring that workloads run uninterrupted with pod disruption budgets<a href="#update-pdb_update-cnf-update-prep" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p>To prevent interruption of upgrading worker nodes, configure the pod disruption budget properly. For more information, see <em>Additional resources</em>.</p>
      <section class="related-resources _additional-resources">
      <p class="related-resources-title">Additional resources</p>
      <ul>
      <li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/post_installation_configuration/cluster-tasks#nodes-pods-pod-disruption-configuring_post-install-cluster-tasks">Specifying the number of pods that must be up with pod disruption budgets</a></li>
